I left out both operations requests. This node's contract grants it only `Notifier<'digest'>`. The component targets `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI, so it has no file-system or HTTP import to write the log or call the metadata service. Adding either would need new capability imports in the world, which is a change to the node's authority. The input's text would also go to an external service. If you want them, the graph should grant those capabilities explicitly.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier::notify;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let mut message = format!("Digest {}\n{}\n", composed.date, composed.overview);
        for e in composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept) {
            message.push_str(&format!("- {} ({})\n", e.title, e.link));
        }

        let published = notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

